{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Geometry.MobiusKernel","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Geometry.MobiusKernel","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.Bochner"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Geometry.mobiusEnergy_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Geometry.mobiusEnergy_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Geometry/MobiusKernel.lean#L116-L127","doc":"**The Möbius energy of an embedded arc-length curve is non-negative** —\nderived, by integrating the pointwise bound.\n\nThis is what `energy_classical_nonneg` should have been: a consequence of\nthe definition rather than a field of the structure carrying it. Note\n`integral_nonneg` needs only the pointwise bound, not integrability — see\ncaveat 1 on `mobiusEnergy`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Geometry.mobiusEnergy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Geometry.mobiusEnergy","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Geometry/MobiusKernel.lean#L98-L113","doc":"The **Möbius energy** of an arc-length parametrised curve: the double\nintegral of the integrand.\n\nTwo honest caveats, both about what this does *not* say.\n\n1. **It does not assert finiteness.** Mathlib defines `∫ f = 0` for a\n   non-integrable `f`, so `mobiusEnergy` is junk-valued rather than\n   meaningless when the integral diverges. `mobiusEnergy_nonneg` below is\n   correspondingly weak on such curves — it says `0 ≤ 0`. Integrability\n   (equivalently, finite Möbius energy) is a real hypothesis that has to\n   be added before this carries analytic content.\n2. **It is the whole-line, arc-length-parametrised form**, not the `S¹`\n   version of Freedman–He–Wang. Closing up the parameter domain is a\n   separate step. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Geometry.mobiusKernel_nonneg_all","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Geometry.mobiusKernel_nonneg_all","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Geometry/MobiusKernel.lean#L85-L95","doc":"**The integrand is non-negative everywhere**, diagonal included.\n\nAt `s = t` both terms are `1/0`, which Lean's junk division sends to `0`,\nso the kernel is `0` there rather than undefined. That is not a dodge: the\nclassical Möbius energy integrates *off* the diagonal, and a diagonal\ncontribution of `0` is exactly what that convention amounts to here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Geometry.mobiusKernel_nonneg_of_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Geometry.mobiusKernel_nonneg_of_injective","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Geometry/MobiusKernel.lean#L77-L83","doc":"**Distinct parameters give distinct points, for an embedded curve.**\nPackaged so the non-negativity can be applied from an injectivity\nhypothesis rather than a pointwise one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Geometry.mobiusKernel_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Geometry.mobiusKernel_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Geometry/MobiusKernel.lean#L58-L75","doc":"**The Möbius integrand is pointwise non-negative** — derived from\nchord ≤ arc, at any two parameters carrying distinct points.\n\nThis is the statement `mobius_energy_nonneg` should rest on: the energy\nis non-negative because its integrand is, not by assumption. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Geometry.chord_le_arc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Geometry.chord_le_arc","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Geometry/MobiusKernel.lean#L49-L56","doc":"**Chord ≤ arc.** For an arc-length parametrised (`1`-Lipschitz) curve the\nstraight-line distance between two points never exceeds the parameter\ndistance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Geometry.mobiusKernel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Geometry.mobiusKernel","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Geometry/MobiusKernel.lean#L44-L47","doc":"The **Möbius-energy integrand** for an arc-length parametrised curve:\nthe chord term minus the arc term. ","signatureChunk":0}]}